WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.150
It's been a while, Zenigata.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.770
Knowing you, you'll be 
worrying about me needlessly,

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.500
so I will bring you up to date.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.030
I'm attending school now.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.260
A boarding school.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:19.370
It's safe, old-fashioned, and you get three 
square meals a day without having to ask.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:24.170
The lessons here are as basic 
as I thought they'd be.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:25.690
As for friends...

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.250
Hey, new girl.

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:32.660
Would you like to eat with us?

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.110
Thank you.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.170
There's only room for three 
on this bench, though...

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.370
Hello, Underworld.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:46.760
Roll SSL back to version 2.0.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:51.120
Run an attack script on the 
weakness in their HTTPS protocol.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:49.120
What the...

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:51.130
A chant, maybe?

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.880
Analyze video footage.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:02.730
There's space over by the garden.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.280
How do you know?

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.790
The security here is full of holes.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:11.450
You mean, you're some kind of... hacker?!

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:17.060
As for friends...

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.360
I still haven't made any.

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:26.380
Stop!

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.800
What are you <i>thinking</i>?!

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.380
What nutcase goes around shooting 
a bow and arrow on school grounds?!

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.280
What a savage...

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:58.380
Let's get out of here.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.810
Search for "crow, corpse, hanging."

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:09.540
Did you say something?

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:11.470
That's to keep other crows away, isn't it?

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:12.760
Yes.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.920
They cause havoc in the flowerbeds.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.590
You don't care if those 
other girls got the wrong idea?

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.300
I'm almost certain they thought 
you were going to <i>eat</i> the crow.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.030
You were under the same 
mistaken impression, weren't you?

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:32.250
I am the only one who 
decides what brings me joy.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:38.000
It doesn't matter what other people 
think, as long as I am satisfied.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.470
You know what? You're absolutely right.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.980
<b>The Bow, The Princess,
 and the Terrorist</b>

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.750
The Bloody Teardrop?

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.860
Hell of a name for a necklace.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:40.190
For six-hundred years, it's been passed 
down through the Padar royal family.

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:44.010
Six-hundred years of blood and tears, huh?

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:48.410
And at the moment, it's in the hands of 
the current king's daughter, Princess Dolma.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.480
She's currently away from home, 
attending a school in Annecy.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:01.200
Wow, all the same outfit.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:04.020
You really like that look, dontcha?

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:05.540
Please...

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:08.090
Call it my "style."

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:10.790
All righty, then.

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:23.020
Maybe all the blood and tears it has 
bathed in are what makes it so beautiful...

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:25.720
Ms. Suzuki!

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.290
Sorry for the holdup!

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:28.860
It's all right.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:34.500
Apparently, it's true!

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:40.600
Here we have the courtyard, which you can 
use as a shortcut to get to the auditorium.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:43.060
It's lovely.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.280
Just what you'd expect to find 
in such a prestigious school.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.470
What's that smoke?

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:50.570
Is there a fire?

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.710
What the heck?

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:52.490
No way!

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:02.580
And that's Princess Dolma?

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:04.660
Her reputation precedes her, I see.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:08.080
She's not exactly what 
I'd call a troublemaker...

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.080
But she certainly stands out.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:12.480
Oh!

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:14.630
And that's...

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:16.600
Oh, she transferred here recently.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:20.130
Rumors abound that she's
 a hacker. Another odd one.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:25.100
Two oddballs... Maybe that's
 why they've bonded.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:46.470
T-minus five. Everyone, prepare to move out.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:06.110
Sorry to trouble you, 
but we need directions...

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:09.150
This is private property. 
You'll have to turn back.

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:15.900
Zero hour. Commence the operation.

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:38.620
Hello, Underworld. Search for "AB Tourist."

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.150
2G and 3G are both down?

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.130
The signal's being blocked?

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:59.960
This school is now under the control 
of the Whales of Liberation.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:03.410
Everyone, put your hands behind your heads.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.950
Do as we say and we won't kill you.

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:11.950
Is Amy Enan here?

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:15.340
On your feet. You're a special case.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.760
Move it!

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:18.080
Ami!

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:20.850
Bitch!

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:21.310
Dolma!

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.190
Where are you hiding?!

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:35.400
Dolma!

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:41.030
Wuh... Why?

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.580
Isn't anyone at Amy's school picking up?

00:08:57.580 --> 00:09:00.430
I'm pretty sure this is 
the right number, too...

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:02.450
Why don't you just shoot them an e-mail?

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:05.560
No. I have to thank her teachers directly.

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:07.440
Like you're her father?

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.720
Still no answer...

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:40.790
There it is.

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:44.320
So that's where we'll find 
the princess and her loot?

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:45.510
As well as Amy.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:51.830
Sorry, but the road's closed!

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:54.040
You folks have business at the school?

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:57.250
Nah, at the museum up ahead.

00:09:57.250 --> 00:10:03.230
I see. Well, I'm real sorry, 
but there's no way through here.

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:05.040
Aw, shucks.

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:06.260
Sorry again!

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:13.310
Hey, what was that about a museum?

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:17.810
The guards at the gate who were there 
when I dropped Amy off aren't there now.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:21.800
Those guys were packing some serious heat.

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:22.580
And look at that.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.150
The signal's being blocked?

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:27.780
Looks like trouble found us again.

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:32.080
With all the curtains drawn, 
they could've shot up the place by now.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:33.300
Are we turning back?

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.810
Surely you jest.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:38.270
Time to do what thieves do best and sneak in.

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:56.840
C-Could you at least let the students go?

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:57.850
Shut the hell up!

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:02.860
I-I'm so sorry!

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:05.350
Violence and blood tend to freak me out...

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:10.680
They took a group of students 
earlier, didn't they?

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:14.880
Huh? Oh, I believe they were 
all daughters of powerful people.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.410
Maybe they're going to ransom them?

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:22.630
Excuse me...

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:23.400
What is it?

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:25.930
Could I please go to the restroom?

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:39.090
We're about to shoot a hostage video.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:42.430
A script's been prepared, 
so make sure you focus on your delivery.

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:47.940
Once the government releases our 
comrades, you'll all be set free.

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:49.280
That's...

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:51.730
What if the government 
doesn't release them?

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.800
Now, who should we start with?

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:58.680
Where is Ami Enan?

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:02.680
The hacker girl we highlighted in the intel.

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:04.410
The former black hat.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:13.340
We are not equals here.

00:12:13.340 --> 00:12:17.450
I give the orders, and you take them.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:26.750
<i>They gagged me instead of blindfolding me...</i>

00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:29.720
<i>They must know who I am.</i>

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:30.970
<i>But how?</i>

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:44.490
But I'm excited.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:48.740
I see. Well, that's good.

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:52.710
<i>Lupin... I'm alive.</i>

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:54.250
<i>And this is exciting.</i>

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:08.250
<i>First, I need to get free.</i>

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:18.030
These ropes are so tight... 
Could you untie me?

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:18.780
No chance.

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:24.060
Please? If I'm all tied up...

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:26.280
we won't be able to have any <i>fun</i>.

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:27.790
Well, in the case...

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:33.880
How about I have <i>my</i> fun first?

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:40.290
And if you do a good job, 
I'll think about untying you.

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:51.660
Ow.

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:54.740
So we meet again.

00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:57.520
You know, I did quite well 
out of that Lupin Game.

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:00.340
Fujiko Mine?!

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:02.020
Wanna lend me a hand?

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:06.860
Don't you want to rescue Princess Dolma?

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.210
What are you after?

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:12.560
I have a hard time believing 
you're doing this out of kindness.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:15.300
I want the necklace that's in her possession.

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:17.570
You want me to help you steal it?!

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:22.080
Now, now. If you're all tied up, 
you can't have any "fun," can you?

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:28.900
You know, kids shouldn't be 
in such a hurry to grow up.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:30.580
Shut the hell up, you witch!

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.290
Let's do a trade.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:36.590
Her life for her necklace.

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:38.840
Which is more important?

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:44.100
I want more than just Dolma. 
You have to help me save the others, too.

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:04.260
Nicely done, Goemon.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:08.710
They've got people posted 
all around, not just indoors.

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:12.420
We're dealing with 
a professional outfit here.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:15.920
Use the security cameras 
to find the hostages,

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:17.910
and map the terrorists' locations.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.690
No one in the music room.

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:24.110
One terrorist in the stairwell on the 
third floor of the western building.

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:26.520
Two in Classroom 1B...

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:29.740
There! Four in the principal's office.

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:37.110
Father! You mustn't give into their 
demands out of concern for me!

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:37.490
Quiet!

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:44.190
You <i>do</i> know this isn't a live stream, right?
 We can just do another take.

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:47.760
I won't say what you want, even if you do!

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:50.630
It'd be a shame to lose a card 
like the Princess of Padar, but...

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:55.700
maybe this'll make the others fall into line 
and it won't seem like such a waste.

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:00.140
We've got a runner.

00:16:01.970 --> 00:16:04.350
A female teacher by the name of Suzuki.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:06.650
She got loose after being 
escorted to the bathroom.

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:09.730
That's the teacher who 
just started working here.

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:11.900
Notify all units in the school grounds.

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:14.120
Get out there and look for her, Adel.

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:14.910
Right.

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:17.300
Let me save you the trouble.

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:31.690
I came here to negotiate.

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:38.130
Well, aren't you a cutie?

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:43.300
Come on. Stop glaring at me like that.

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:45.010
It's pretty obvious that I'm unarmed.

00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:47.410
You mentioned negotiations.

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:49.530
Are you here to beg for your life? Or...

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:51.930
Teaching is just my cover story.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:57.520
In reality, I'm a bodyguard employed by 
the Padar Kingdom to protect the princess.

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:06.760
There's one thing in particular 
these terrorists want.

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:09.690
To have their friends released?

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:11.790
That's the best-case scenario, sure.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:16.710
But even if the trade falls through, 
and even if they all end up dead,

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:20.170
they succeed in their aims as long as
a bunch of students get killed.

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:21.760
Why?

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:24.200
It's called "terrorism" for a reason.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:28.690
They want to scare the world into changing.

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:32.340
My guess is there's a bomb 
somewhere in the auditorium.

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:35.130
Can you imagine the reaction?

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:36.190
We need to disarm it!

00:17:36.190 --> 00:17:38.570
Stealing the detonator would do the trick.

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:39.820
Where is it?

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.660
I'm about to go ask them.

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:44.210
There's no way they'd tell you!

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:51.040
You'd be surprised... just how <i>simple </i>men are.

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:56.330
There are other Padar agents on the campus.

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:57.730
You're bluffing.

00:17:57.730 --> 00:18:00.130
We won't get in your way.

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:04.220
But only... if you release the princess.

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:12.730
Y'know, this bozo might act tough, 
but he's really just a scaredy-cat.

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:13.990
What?!

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:17.230
<i>People like him are too paranoid to trust.</i>

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:21.750
Which is why they'd never trust 
anyone else with their secret weapon.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:22.860
You!

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:23.790
Amy!

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:24.550
It's Ami!

00:18:29.980 --> 00:18:30.800
Leader!

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:33.490
Get the lights back on! 
Otherwise, we'll shoot each other!

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:46.140
All sorted.

00:18:57.560 --> 00:18:59.160
You saved us.

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:01.710
I had no idea I had such a skilled bodyguard.

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:05.200
Oh, that was a lie.

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:08.720
I'm Fujiko Mine.

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:11.640
A woman who's always loyal to her desires.

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:16.980
What the—

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:26.180
Okay!

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.970
Looks like we're about done here.

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:32.650
Hey, Amy! You over there? It's Lupin!

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:34.720
Your good, old Uncle Lupin!

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:37.720
Dolma!

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:39.000
Ami!

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:42.750
Oh, I get it now! You were 
the one who turned off the lights!

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.360
Did they hurt you?

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:45.480
What about you?

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:51.970
Called it.

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:55.060
Everyone! Are you... okay?

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.250
Did you do all this?

00:19:57.810 --> 00:19:59.960
That hussy over there saved them.

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:03.260
Get away from that man!

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:10.140
Princess Dolma, these women are thieves.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:11.520
You cannot trust them.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:12.680
Dolma!

00:20:12.680 --> 00:20:13.640
Who are you?

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:16.310
I'm with the Special Activities...

00:20:16.670 --> 00:20:19.390
Well, let's just say, the CIA. 
The name's McGuire.

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:31.340
That's...

00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:42.230
Please, Princess Dolma... 
you must come with me to save Padar.

00:22:16.300 --> 00:22:17.620
Zenigata here.

00:22:17.620 --> 00:22:19.380
Serves you right, Lupin!

00:22:19.380 --> 00:22:21.400
Your score got away.

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:24.030
Princess Dolma's been replaced, 
but the real one's returning to Padar,

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:27.200
a kingdom caught between 
tradition and modernity.

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:29.680
Wait, Lupin sent his calling 
card to the royal palace?!

00:22:29.680 --> 00:22:32.670
The scumbag must still 
be after the necklace!

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:35.320
But how will you get into a royal palace...

00:22:35.320 --> 00:22:37.950
that's remained impenetrable 
for six-hundred years, Lupin?!

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:40.250
Next time: How To Steal a Kingdom.

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:44.950
<b>How To Steal A Kingdom</b>

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:44.120
Bring the car around, Yata! 
We're off to Padar!
